    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="0861" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2748: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the American Delegation to the Seventh
                            International Conference of American States</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-05T18:00:00-05:00">December 5, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Your No. 20, December 2, 8 p.m.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d696-f1"/> As of
                    possible interest in connection with the proposal of the Haitian delegation for
                    withdrawal <pb facs="0862" n="774" xml:id="pg774"/> of American control over
                    Haitian finances through the designation of the National Bank of Haiti in place
                    of the Financial Adviser-General Receiver, you are informed that the National
                    City Bank has offered to sell the entire capital stock of the National Bank of
                    Haiti to the Haitian Government at a figure understood to be in the neighborhood
                    of two million dollars.</p>
                <p>The Department is not informed as to the attitude of the Haitian Government
                    toward the offer. The Financial Adviser-General Receiver has reported to the
                    Legation that he would regard the acquisition of the Bank as not being in the
                    interest of Haiti’s finances.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d696-f1" n="81" xml:id="d696-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 85, December 4, 3 p.m., to the Minister in Haiti, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
